1,Pangwali,https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Pangwali.htm,"Pangwali is spoken by approximately 18,000 speakers in Chamba district, Pangi sub-district; Lahaul Spiti district, Udaipur on Chenab river to Chamba border at Purthi, Himachal Pradesh state and Doda district in Jammu and Kashmir state, India.",Pangwali,Indo-European
2,Pangwali language,https://www.omniglot.com/writing/pangwali.htm,"Pangwali is a Western Pahari language spoken mainly in Himachal Pradesh state in northern India by about 18,700 people.Pangwali is a member of the North-Western branch of the Western Pahari group of Indo-Aryan languages.",Pangwali,Indo-European
3,Pangwali,https://docs.verbix.com/EndangeredLanguages/Pangwali,"Alternate names: Satlaj, Pahari, Pangi, Pangwali Pahari. Language code: pgg. Language family: Indo-European, Indo-Iranian, Indo-Aryan, Northern zone, Western Pahari (SIL classification). Number of speakers: 17,000. Vulnerability: Threatened.",Pangwali,Indo-European
